{"name":"Award Winning White","hex":"#fef0de","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"award","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A judgment, sentence, or final decision. Specifically: The decision of arbitrators in a case submitted.","The paper containing the decision of arbitrators; that which is warded."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To determine; to make or grant an award.","To give (an award)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/award"},{"term":"winning","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["present participle and gerund of win"]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["That constitutes a win.","That leads to success."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/winning"},{"term":"white","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Bright and colourless; reflecting equal quantities of all frequencies of visible light.","Of or relating to Europeans or those of European descent, regardless if their skin has cool or warm undertones."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of snow or milk; the color of light containing equal amounts of all visible wavelengths.","A person of European descent with light-colored skin."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/white"}],"entries":[{"title":"Award","blocks":[{"text":"An award, sometimes called a distinction, is given to a recipient as a token of recognition of excellence in a certain field. When the token is a medal, ribbon or other item designed for wearing, it is known as a decoration."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/NJROTC_Awards.jpg/330px-NJROTC_Awards.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Award","wikidata":"Q618779"},{"title":"White","blocks":[{"text":"White is the lightest color and is achromatic. It is the color of objects such as snow, chalk, and milk, and is the opposite of black. White objects fully reflect and scatter all the visib